course: dictionary
lesson: 12113
title: Collectively: all together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how a group does something. Collectively is one of them. It means all together, as a group, rather than each person alone. «The children collectively collected 50 cans for the food bank.» Nobody collected 50 cans alone. The whole class added their cans into one total.
explain: Look at the words around it. Words like team, group, class, family or everyone often show that collectively is coming. «The team collectively scored 30 goals this season.» The goals belong to the team as a whole, not to one player.
explain: Collectively can also mean counting everyone or everything together. In maths, «collectively they have 40 marbles» means that if you add up all their marbles, the total is 40. A quick check: swap in together or altogether. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found its meaning.
fact: Collectively means all together, as a group.
fact: Collectively also means counting everyone or everything together.
fact: «Collectively they have 40 marbles» means their marbles add up to 40 in total.
fact: Other words with a similar meaning are together, altogether and in all.
fact: In citizenship lessons, people collectively decide things by voting as a whole group.
exercise: «The children collectively collected 50 cans for the food bank.» What does collectively mean here? | Very quickly | Each child alone, one at a time | *All together, as a group | Without any help
exercise: «Collectively they have 40 marbles.» What does this sentence tell us? | Each child has 40 marbles | They gave away 40 marbles | They lost all their marbles | *Their marbles add up to 40 in total
exercise: «The villagers collectively decided to build a new park.» Which word could replace collectively without changing the meaning? | loudly | quietly | alone | *together
test: Ella says, «The class collectively read 200 pages this term.» What does collectively mean? | They read very slowly | The class read nothing at all | *The whole class added their reading together | Each child read a page alone
test: Which word is closest in meaning to collectively? | Loudly | *Altogether | Often | Alone
exam: Which sentence shows the whole group doing something together? | Jo collectively lost her pencil | *The players collectively won the match | Dad collectively drove the car alone | Sam collectively ate all the sweets himself
